-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  dir_exeicon_err_decode.pcpp - break step of dir_exeicon_linux.pcpp: an icon
  file that exists but holds no image (this very file): the compiler cannot
  decode it to build it in, so nothing is built (the report names the file
  and the decoder's reason)

  How to check, from repo\bin (the Linux target only: on Windows the icon is
  stamped after the build):
    pcpp res\tests\dir_exeicon_err_decode.pcpp -t x86_64-linux-gnu
  The marked line reports that code; nothing else is reported.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe dir_exeicon_err_decode;
@exeicon "$P:res/tests/dir_exeicon_err_decode.pcpp"; // ERROR CMP0008@10: cannot build the icon

begin
end.
